{"kind":"assert","text":"Correction to my approval of head e1fa1f3ada88cf1a40e852e19a3f91ae08423d89. The verdict stands; one supporting claim in its architecture paragraph was overstated and should not be relied on.\n\nI wrote that internal/kernel carries 'exactly the two halves the page defines' for docs/reference/event-identifiers.md. That is wrong as a statement of fact. internal/kernel/kernel.go and checkpoint.go contain no '#' at all: the kernel never composes, splits, or observes the compound \u003cworkroom\u003e#\u003cevent\u003e identifier. What the kernel does own, and what makes it a defensible rather than an exact anchor, is the substrate the page's definition refers to — the genesis descriptor and its ObjectFormat, and the sequence ref layout at kernel.go:286, func Ref(genesis string) string { return \"refs/seq/\" + genesis }. It also builds and compares the single-part typed OID \"git:\"+format+\":\"+genesis as a signed target at kernel.go:1154 and checkpoint.go:262.\n\nThe compound identifier is constructed in exactly one place, internal/app/app.go:1077-1079, Workspace.EventID, which joins the two typed OIDs with '#'. The half form git:\u003cformat\u003e:\u003coid\u003e is built and parsed in internal/gitstore/gitstore.go:90-104. The canonical form is enforced by regex in internal/docset/docset.go:50-53 and again in cmd/gitseq-mcp/main.go:1472-1475 and ui/src/lib/interaction.ts:119.\n\nConsequence for the merged set, stated plainly so nobody has to rediscover it: event-identifiers.md will flare on kernel merges, including ones that do not touch the identifier such as checkpointing or backpressure, and will not flare on a change to the composition at app.go:1077. That is a looser coupling than the other nine pages in this head received, where the new basis is the component that actually carries the documented behaviour.\n\nThis does not reverse the approval and is not a merge blocker. The head satisfies every condition the review request set: internal/kernel is a real single tree path, live and non-stale at the exact head, and semantically related to what the page defines, and the page moves from a comma-joined pseudo-path that could never flare and contained no implementation at all. Tightening one anchor is follow-up work, not a defect in this repair.\n\nRecommended follow-up, under its own request: add internal/app to the bases of docs/reference/event-identifiers.md, and consider internal/gitstore for the typed-OID half. I verified the live non-stale anchors available for that work at the time of writing — internal/app: git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:e015e6b1f152a008e0bf8fd3d16e22ae7c2b147a at commit f52630d2; internal/gitstore: git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:7755a1195e83805be2a8fa5023c70f609891ec40 at commit cbddb3d8. Note that most artifacts at internal/app are retired; resolve against the projection rather than assuming."}